    "# FPrint-FIDO2 Bridge — Build Plan\n\n## What We're Building\nA software FIDO2 authenticator that uses your laptop's fingerprint sensor for user verification, appearing as a real security key to browsers.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n- Browsers support WebAuthn/FIDO2 natively — no extensions needed\n- Your fingerprint sensor works but can't talk FIDO2 directly\n- We bridge the gap entirely in software\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nFirefox/Chrome\n     │  WebAuthn API\n     ▼\n/dev/uhid  ◄── our daemon (virtual FIDO2 HID device)\n     │\n     ├── CTAP2 protocol handler (parse browser requests)\n     ├── Credential store (encrypted local file)\n     └── fprintd D-Bus (fingerprint verify instead of PIN)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Components\n\n### 1. Virtual HID Device\n- Open `/dev/uhid`, register as a FIDO2 HID device\n- Browser discovers it like a USB security key\n- Library: `uhid-python`\n\n### 2. CTAP2 Protocol Handler\n- Handle `authenticatorMakeCredential` — register on a website\n- Handle `authenticatorGetAssertion` — login to a website\n- Handle `authenticatorGetInfo` — tell browser our capabilities\n- Library: `python-fido2` (server-side, reuse its CBOR/CTAP2 parsing)\n\n### 3. Fingerprint Verification\n- When browser asks for user verification (UV flag)\n- Call `fprintd` via D-Bus → user touches sensor → verified\n- Fallback: PIN if finger fails N times\n\n### 4. Credential Storage\n- Store private keys + metadata per site in `~/.local/share/fido2-fprint/credentials.db`\n- Encrypted with a master key derived from login keyring\n\n---\n\n## Tech Stack\n- **Python** — fast to build, `python-fido2` saves weeks of work\n- **cryptography** — key generation (ES256 / P-256)\n- **dbus-python** — talk to fprintd\n- **uhid-python** — virtual HID device\n- **sqlite3** — credential storage (stdlib)\n\n---\n\n## Build Order\n\n| Step | What | Why first |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| 1 | Virtual HID device that browser detects | Proves the approach works |\n| 2 | `authenticatorGetInfo` response | Browser knows our capabilities |\n| 3 | `authenticatorMakeCredential` | Register on a site |\n| 4 | Fingerprint verification integration | Core feature |\n| 5 | `authenticatorGetAssertion` | Actually log in |\n| 6 | Credential storage | Persist across reboots |\n| 7 | udev rules + systemd service | Auto-start, no root needed |\n\n---\n\n## What We Won't Support (to keep it buildable)\n- PIN (fingerprint only)\n- NFC/BLE transport (HID only)\n- Enterprise attestation (self-signed only)\n- Multi-device sync\n\n---\n\n## End Result\n- Register fingerprint on GitHub, Google, etc. as a security key\n- Touch sensor to log in\n- Works in Firefox and Chrome\n- No cloud, no hardware dongle, fully local\n\n---\n\nReady to start with Step 1? Also — Python fine, or do you want Rust?\n[Tool uses: none]",
